From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Project Luma <builds@project-luma.local>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 16:40:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] luma: Beam finds Filer's places

Typing "Applications", "apps", "trash" or "bin" found nothing: Beam had
providers for apps, files and Settings pages, but none for the places in
Filer's sidebar, and Filer's own search provider (which Beam replaces)
never offered them either.

- lumaFilerPlaces.js reads luma-search's filer-places.json (shared with
  the Python service) and resolves Home, Recent, Starred, Applications,
  Desktop and the standard folders, Network, Trash, System Disk and the
  user's bookmarks, in Filer's translated labels. Places Filer would not
  show (Recent with recent files off, System Disk in personal-storage
  mode, a missing folder) are not offered.
- lumaPlacesSearch.js ranks them by name and everyday words ("apps",
  "bin", "other locations") with the Settings-page model and opens Filer
  at the location its sidebar opens (applications:///, trash:///, ...).
- A standard folder found both as a place and as a folder shows once.
---
